{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513662-no-need-to-kungfu-fighting-they-re-not-that-serious","id":1513662,"title":"No need to Kungfu Fighting, they're not that serious","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-02T09:48:28-07:00","id":1513662,"title":"No need to Kungfu Fighting, they're not that serious","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/481568210043273237/1114167658485665793/IMG_9382.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/481568210043273237/1114167658485665793/IMG_9382.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/481568210043273237/1114167658485665793/IMG_9382.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> </div> <hr /><br /> So in the wuxia stories that I read it's all about martial arts, obviously, basically since you have to learn a MA from a manual someone wrote (which usually there is only one) or learn from a teacher in a sect which leads to all kinds of drama, like sneaking into the Shaolin Hidden Sutra Tower to steal their manuals, or marrying your daughter into a family so she can steal those fancy MA books, and even going crazy from practicing a MA wrong since you only have the lower Sutra of the MA when you tried to murder your sifu to steal his books.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Exalted seems to completely lack these kinds of plot since MA are so common, or rather they are not limited to a sect so there's no need to do all of these elaborate plots to steal a MA, the local martial art hall don't want to teach you Snake Style? There are 300 more guys out there who can. Plus one of the reasons why these wuxia scenarios happen is due to the MA the character wants to steal is really really powerful, meanwhile Exalted is a ttrpg that requires all MA to be equal in power so like, why jump into a cliff trying to get a burning manual of Dreaming Courtesan Style when it's really not any stronger than other MA, plus the whole aforementioned thing about dozen of people who can teach you that style.<br /> <br /> I wonder what other kinds of martial arts drama that I can have instead in Exalted since I can't exactly use the one that I learn from wuxia novels at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T11:18:22-07:00","id":1513672,"title":"","content":"Exalted's always had a somewhat troubled history with how well it emulates Wuxia tropes rather than being fantasy super heroes. I know that part of the purpose of Solar (or appropriate splat) Experience was to encourage PCs to work with the Storyteller and engage with the potential difficulties of learning martial arts or sorcery rather than trying to skip past it to instant mastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:26:12-07:00","id":1513678,"title":"","content":"About the power level issue, MA are generally valued not necessarily from a level power but because they can do things that your own Charms can't, the Gazelle-Carp shape capping off DPC being a standout example for non-shapeshifters. Obviously, earlier editions Dragon-Blooded or 2e Dragon Kings out to bolster their less powerful stuff with Celestial styles are an exception, but Solars and Abyssals learning SMA are in it for versatility, because they could just straight up murder their enemies and end things a lot faster, albeit with many more... complications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:36:48-07:00","id":1513683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513662-no-need-to-kungfu-fighting-they-re-not-that-serious?p=1513672#post1513672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted's always had a somewhat troubled history with how well it emulates Wuxia tropes rather than being fantasy super heroes. I know that part of the purpose of Solar (or appropriate splat) Experience was to encourage PCs to work with the Storyteller and engage with the potential difficulties of learning martial arts or sorcery rather than trying to skip past it to instant mastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, natural ups and downs from the fact of Exalted being a setting where Wuxia is an element of inspiration among several and not a Wuxia setting front and center, what might require some considerable changes in tone and mechanics i dare say, with the idea of essence manipulation in itself springing from martial arts practices, division of styles or at least charms connected to them into tiers or circles like in late 1e and 2nd ed (and we have backpedaled from in 3e) among other things.<br /> <br /> It's a far from simple issue to adress imho, though i have toyed slightly with a sorcerous initiation with a connection to martial arts, inner alchemy and evocations as one possible path to bring some of the tropes resonant to the genre into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T16:51:16-07:00","id":1513727,"title":"","content":"Vigilantism, often vengeful, is the \u2018xia\u2019 of \u2018wuxia\u2019, so there\u2019s that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T08:34:29-07:00","id":1513954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513662-no-need-to-kungfu-fighting-they-re-not-that-serious#post1513662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the wuxia stories that I read it's all about martial arts, obviously, basically since you have to learn a MA from a manual someone wrote (which usually there is only one) or learn from a teacher in a sect which leads to all kinds of drama, like sneaking into the Shaolin Hidden Sutra Tower to steal their manuals, or marrying your daughter into a family so she can steal those fancy MA books, and even going crazy from practicing a MA wrong since you only have the lower Sutra of the MA when you tried to murder your sifu to steal his books.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Exalted seems to completely lack these kinds of plot since MA are so common</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some of those plots or things resembling them show up in the history parts of the write-ups for several published Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">rather they are not limited to a sect so there's no need to do all of these elaborate plots to steal a MA, the local martial art hall don't want to teach you Snake Style? There are 300 more guys out there who can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is going on a distant pilgrimage to find an alternative teacher to spite the people more familiar to you who refused to provide teaching not compatible with the sorts of stories you're talking about?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus one of the reasons why these wuxia scenarios happen is due to the MA the character wants to steal is really really powerful, meanwhile Exalted is a ttrpg that requires all MA to be equal in power so like, why jump into a cliff trying to get a burning manual of Dreaming Courtesan Style when it's really not any stronger than other MA</div> </div> </div> </div>Well what's the metric along which one compares Dreaming Pearl Courtesan, Black Claw, and Tiger?<br /> <br /> Some of these are just putting your personal spin on killing (or at least expanding the range of your tactical options), while some provide methods you wouldn't otherwise have that can be employed in a context where you would be otherwise limited.<br /> <br /> You might never be learning the Five Point Palm Exploding Heart Technique so you can single-handedly slay a monastery, but sometimes you're looking for the greater range of capabilities that will give you an edge, sometimes you want to be especially good at fighting and killing with secrecy or in a social situation, and sometimes you can be very invested in things like fighting while maintaining the facade of innocence or incinerating the wicked or other things that make a statement.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T09:48:43-07:00","id":1513957,"title":"","content":"You are talking about the traditional &quot;Wuxia&quot; or &quot;Martial heroes&quot; stories, like Legend of the Condor Heroes and Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon. And agreed. Exalted is not really about singular heroes of martial arts living at the edge of society and battling each other for dominance in their own little society within society.<br /> <br /> However, the martial arts stories have in some form been a staple of Chinese literature for over 2000 years and they have many genres and many iterations. Many of them still debated this day among literature students and professors. Exalted pays homage to the subgenre of martial arts stories: Xianxia. That is: martial arts stories with mythic powers, gods, demons, heavens, hells, mythic weapons, world cracking powers and struggle of good and evil. These stories are considered martial arts stories and some Wuxia novels might have elements that are more Xianxia and vice versa. Exalted is perfectly within those kind of genres.<br /> <br /> Xianxia doesn't really deal with competing schools of martial arts, the martial arts societies or some martial arts manual either. At least they are not the usual tropes in Xianxia stories. Yet Xianxia is still considered part of the martial arts genre and is heavily influenced by Taoist, Buddhist and dozens of other philosophies and folklore. Many of them dealing in supernatural and mythical. And it still has martial arts schools, philosophical nigh wizard-like martial arts societies and secret maneuvers and...well to be honest attacks that look much like &quot;spells&quot; to me. <br /> <br /> For reference I recommend Legend of the Swordsmen of the Mountains of Su, Demi-Gods and Semi-Devils and Legend of the White Snake not to mention the dozens of film adaptations of all of these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11221-turtleking","user":"Turtleking","date":". 06-05-2023, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11221-turtleking","name":"Turtleking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T10:42:02-07:00","id":1514021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513662-no-need-to-kungfu-fighting-they-re-not-that-serious?p=1513954#post1513954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think some of those plots or things resembling them show up in the history parts of the write-ups for several published Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is going on a distant pilgrimage to find an alternative teacher to spite the people more familiar to you who refused to provide teaching not compatible with the sorts of stories you're talking about?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, since those wuxia plots are so *very* dramatic which gonna feels very weird since Exalted MA doesn\u2019t seem like it\u2019s designed to accommodate those plots thanks to being a trrpg.<br /> <br /> Though I just realized that Artifacts are doing a better job for at generating wuxia soap-opera plots, nobody gonna break into The Castle of 1000+ DEF to steal some book that teach Snake Style, but someone definitely will if there is an artifact inside O3O","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T10:49:57-07:00","id":1514023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513662-no-need-to-kungfu-fighting-they-re-not-that-serious?p=1513672#post1513672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted's always had a somewhat troubled history with how well it emulates Wuxia tropes rather than being fantasy super heroes. I know that part of the purpose of Solar (or appropriate splat) Experience was to encourage PCs to work with the Storyteller and engage with the potential difficulties of learning martial arts or sorcery rather than trying to skip past it to instant mastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does feel strange that Exalted looks at the training/cultivating chapters in these stories and go \u201cCan we skip these part?\u201d, I guess there just aren\u2019t many interesting mechanic that you can hang on training time so Exalted just dump it on downtime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T12:54:55-07:00","id":1514039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513662-no-need-to-kungfu-fighting-they-re-not-that-serious?p=1514021#post1514021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, since those wuxia plots are so *very* dramatic which gonna feels very weird since Exalted MA doesn\u2019t seem like it\u2019s designed to accommodate those plots thanks to being a trrpg.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I think if the story of going to find somebody far away to teach you a style isn't well accommodated then it doesn't matter how many schools there are.<br /> <br /> So I think either another school exists elsewhere and you have to go on a dramatic journey to be taught there <i>or</i> there's only one school within practical reach and it's necessary to find some way to make it acknowledge you, and I'd say either way one has decent story fodder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">nobody gonna break into The Castle of 1000+ DEF to steal some book that teach Snake Style</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not Snake Style specifically, but I feel as though some of this rests on the question of whether it's more important for such a thing to be a source of sheer power or something that the character has a strong personal investment in.<br /> <br /> Although even for Snake Style... I can see certain character types with a particular motive for learning the techniques of going for the armoured warrior and breaking them down with paralysis and poison. It's not ultimate power but self-expression or making a point. The peasant monk who wants to learn particular gruesome methods for tearing down the armoured soldiers of the local magnate to strike a particular note of fear in them.<br /> <br /> But still, you can also be very driven to learn Crane Style for the particular methods of keeping yourself alive without having to strike so violently at your enemy, and juxtaposing combat with negotiation to end hostilities.<br /> <br /> Indeed, thinking about some of this brings to light some of the issue I can take with a setting containing the premise of objectively superior martial arts styles, as I think it can very easily fall away from a varied and interesting set of competing schools and into the one condescendingly superior school against which all others are merely consolation prizes. It seems more diminishing of alternatives than really building up the main one, which can be an issue even in a story focused on just a singular main character. Something like Exalted, where all of these styles have to exist together and be available for players, I think that illustrates its actual weaknesses more than being a format that fails to accommodate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-06-2023, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T15:37:38-07:00","id":1514061,"title":"","content":"i mean as far as training montages go<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Miaf5u4CJ54\" data-code=\"Miaf5u4CJ54\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Miaf5u4CJ54/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I think if you're gonna have a super cool unique talent or style that exists ya'll should make it up yourselves. I think its more unique and would probably encapsulate your characters driving philosophy more tbh.<br /> <br /> I've been doing kung fu for 20 years and tbh once you know the variety you're dealing with, you'll start seeing a lot of movements and intentions repeat themselves. There is a reason that a lot of the concepts and movements you find in Hung Ga also exists in Jow Ga, because these two styles share lineage and one is building off the other. Hung ga also has a lot of its roots in southern shaolin and so on and so on. Martial arts tend to be more of a back and forth, question and answer. Usually someone becomes predominant with a certain method of thinking about fighting, until someone else looks at that style and says &quot;what kind of movements would this style be weak to?&quot; And then usually gets built from there.<br /> <br /> I know its not exactly wuxia themed, but wuxia novels are trying to encapsulate a human experience and then exaggerate it. There is so much you can do with minor tweaks to the current styles and their charms to make each feel unique or create their own individual branches. In this im just saying, homebrew rules will sadly have to be your guiding star for a more unique experience. Plenty of old kung fu movies have great styles and plots for creating your own style, like the five venoms is a classic movie with 5 different styles to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8897-joshopotamus","name":"joshopotamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T16:03:58-07:00","id":1514066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513662-no-need-to-kungfu-fighting-they-re-not-that-serious?p=1514023#post1514023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does feel strange that Exalted looks at the training/cultivating chapters in these stories and go \u201cCan we skip these part?\u201d, I guess there just aren\u2019t many interesting mechanic that you can hang on training time so Exalted just dump it on downtime.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main problem for me is when characters who aren't invested in these narratives actively shit-talk characters who are, mostly because it's <i>so easy</i> for a PC to accidently do a racism there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T01:30:24-07:00","id":1514095,"title":"","content":"I've never really felt like Exalted has done a good job of integrating martial arts into real-world cultures. We don't often get martial arts schools or traditions incorporated into setting chapters in the books, and most martial arts writeups are far more interested in how those fighting arts influence the combat system than how they integrate with people, places, and their cultures.<br /> <br /> The notable exception to this is Wu Jian, which presents rival schools, gangs, multiple martial arts practiced by various sects and factions, which have had a historical influence on their surroundings and are a strong part of the local culture. It's almost like a martial arts quarantine zone where a lot of the usual wuxia tropes are playing out inside a Kowloon-inspired bottle.<br /> <br /> That's annoying to me, and it's been more annoying ever since I read <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/the-centipedes-dilemma-exalted-kung-fu-quest.62815/\" target=\"_blank\">The Centipede's Dilemma</a>, a quest on Sufficient Velocity about martial artists and the quest for martial truth and wholeness. Its portrayal of martial arts as something more well-integrated at the setting level, where your school matters much more than your 'style,' helped cement the image of what Exalted's martial arts could be in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T14:36:24-07:00","id":1514243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513662-no-need-to-kungfu-fighting-they-re-not-that-serious?p=1514095#post1514095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's annoying to me, and it's been more annoying ever since I read <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/the-centipedes-dilemma-exalted-kung-fu-quest.62815/\" target=\"_blank\">The Centipede's Dilemma</a>, a quest on Sufficient Velocity about martial artists and the quest for martial truth and wholeness. Its portrayal of martial arts as something more well-integrated at the setting level, where your school matters much more than your 'style,' helped cement the image of what Exalted's martial arts could be in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Well, it's much like the dilemma of the centipede. If he relaxes and lets things happen, he can walk naturally all day long, his hundred legs not missing a step. But, if he thinks too hard about the complexity of what he's doing, those legs might crash into the teahouse and kill everyone. A valuable lesson.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T12:00:59-07:00","id":1514326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513662-no-need-to-kungfu-fighting-they-re-not-that-serious?p=1514243#post1514243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Well, it's much like the dilemma of the centipede. If he relaxes and lets things happen, he can walk naturally all day long, his hundred legs not missing a step. But, if he thinks too hard about the complexity of what he's doing, those legs might crash into the teahouse and kill everyone. A valuable lesson.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Pedantry that changes nothing about the concept being discussed - centipedes actually have somewhere between 30 and nearly 400 legs, depending on which species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T05:41:07-07:00","id":1514452,"title":"","content":"I am interested in the Sideral companion book, because there is mention there i think of secret techiques? I think exalted COULD do things like &quot;to learn specific MA charms requires a mentor&quot;? The same way it does for SMAs already? (although that's about mentors not about texts again)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T03:01:48-07:00","id":1514675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513662-no-need-to-kungfu-fighting-they-re-not-that-serious#post1513662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the wuxia stories that I read it's all about martial arts, obviously, basically since you have to learn a MA from a manual someone wrote (which usually there is only one) or learn from a teacher in a sect which leads to all kinds of drama, like sneaking into the Shaolin Hidden Sutra Tower to steal their manuals, or marrying your daughter into a family so she can steal those fancy MA books, and even going crazy from practicing a MA wrong since you only have the lower Sutra of the MA when you tried to murder your sifu to steal his books.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Exalted seems to completely lack these kinds of plot since MA are so common, or rather they are not limited to a sect so there's no need to do all of these elaborate plots to steal a MA, the local martial art hall don't want to teach you Snake Style? There are 300 more guys out there who can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm put in mind of Avatar the Last Airbender.<br /> <br /> The titular character and the female lead want to learn the esoteric art of Waterbending.<br /> <br /> There is an entire waterbending civilization. There's a hidden village in a swamp. One of the arch bad-guys has forbidden bloodbending techniques. And there is a scroll of waterbending. The spirit of the moon is a waterbender. The Airbender's past life was a waterbender. And, of course, they practice together and teach each other.<br /> <br /> At no point in the story is learning waterbending treated as trivial, despite these many, many, many methods of learning it. Indeed, travelling to the waterbending civilisation is a major plot point. As is finding the scroll. As is learning the ultimate technique of bloodbending.<br /> <br /> Just because there are lots of alternative teachers, this in no way lessens the drama.<br /> <br /> In essence, if you want to learn Snake Style, travel to the Coiled Viper Dojo. If Ashana Ikatu refuses to train you, go on a quest to find the Hundred Shed Scales manual that teaches Snake Style. Nothing stops your ST saying the manual is incomplete, and though it allows you to master the Form, you must now descend into hell and seek out demon master Suntarankal to complete your training. Then you can return to the Coiled Viper Dojo and finish your feud with Ashana Ikatu.<br /> <br /> That is a perfectly valid Exalted story.<br /> <br /> Now, yes, you can just learn Heaven Thunder Hammer without a teacher and punt Ashana into next week with a single roll, if you don't want to learn Snake Style. But, like, The Bride didn't need to learn the Five Point Palm Exploding Heart Technique: she could have just Killed Bill with an Uzi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-12-2023, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T14:04:35-07:00","id":1514879,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513662-no-need-to-kungfu-fighting-they-re-not-that-serious?p=1514675#post1514675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm put in mind of Avatar the Last Airbender.<br /> <br /> The titular character and the female lead want to learn the esoteric art of Waterbending.<br /> <br /> There is an entire waterbending civilization. There's a hidden village in a swamp. One of the arch bad-guys has forbidden bloodbending techniques. And there is a scroll of waterbending. The spirit of the moon is a waterbender. The Airbender's past life was a waterbender. And, of course, they practice together and teach each other.<br /> <br /> At no point in the story is learning waterbending treated as trivial, despite these many, many, many methods of learning it. Indeed, travelling to the waterbending civilisation is a major plot point. As is finding the scroll. As is learning the ultimate technique of bloodbending.<br /> <br /> Just because there are lots of alternative teachers, this in no way lessens the drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that scarcity it's part of the deal here, trough it was &quot;artificial&quot; to some extent thanks to how <i>avaliabile </i>were these sources<br /> <br /> The waterbending civilization was far away and/or dying, the village was hidden for good reasons, the Airbender was having a hard time accessing past lives, the arch-bad-guy was either unknown or in the future, and the scroll was so important precisely because these alternative teachers weren't exactly <i>there</i><br /> <br /> The drama would have been lessened if the characters just &quot;wanted&quot; to go to the south pole for not-sufficently-dramatic reasons, rather they &quot;needed&quot; to get there because it's where they knew they were going to find what they needed to advance the quest to win the war, restore balance and all that. The scroll was very clearly not good enough, and potential Avatar teachers had a bad habit of being ensnared by the war that was following him like a death cloud.<br /> <br /> ...So, this is something that can be <i>solved trough</i> <i>story</i>, maybe? But one would have to establish the setting so it is <i>actually solved</i> this way...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">eanwhile Exalted seems to completely lack these kinds of plot since MA are so common, or rather they are not limited to a sect so there's no need to do all of these elaborate plots to steal a MA, the local martial art hall don't want to teach you Snake Style? There are 300 more guys out there who can.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would seem that Snake Style it's so common that it can be learnt from anywhere.(in spite of the fact you have to buy an expensive Merit to start with any MA, if I'm not mistaken , right?).<br /> Does it <i>have </i>to be this way?.<br /> <br /> Because if it doesn't have to be this way, then a <i>story </i>doesn't seem <i>impossible </i>, altrough making it worth the while for everyone may be triky: I get that MA aren't gamebreaking by themselves, but a MA focused character will still want to learn some. perhaps several to combo ... so the &quot;quest&quot; it's there as long as not every local guard knows it, and can teach for a penny. Then it just needs to be non-obtrusive for those that<i> aren't</i> on the same boat and it will be OK. Maybe the martial Master, Temple, or Scroll, it's important for <i>other </i>reasons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T13:19:52-07:00","id":1515006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513662-no-need-to-kungfu-fighting-they-re-not-that-serious?p=1514879#post1514879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that scarcity it's part of the deal here, trough it was &quot;artificial&quot; to some extent thanks to how <i>avaliabile </i>were these sources<br /> <br /> It would seem that Snake Style it's so common that it can be learnt from anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are 53 non animal antagonists in the corebook.<br /> 4 of these are martial artists.<br /> None of which are Snake Stylists.<br /> <br /> There are a further 76 antagonists in Adversaries of the Righteous.<br /> 6 of these are martial artists.<br /> <i>One</i> of whom is a Snake Stylist.<br /> <br /> Yes, the style &quot;flourishes in dojos of the South and the East&quot; and &quot;its practitioners can be found throughout all of Creation&quot;. Finding a teacher shouldn't require travelling to the opposite end of the world whilst evading a particularly dedicated Fire Aspect and his cool uncle. You absolutely should be able to find a teacher for Snake Style. 100%.<br /> <br /> But it's not like every town guard knows it.\u200b<br /> <br /> If you want to make a story out of learning Snake Style, you can absolutely make a story out of learning Snake Style. Using, near as damn it, the exact same plot beats Avatar used to introduce &quot;artificial scarcity&quot;. It is in no way ubiquitous. You can easily have an entire chronicle where you never meet a snake stylist.<br /> <br /> (There or there abouts. I've had a long day and a lot of pain meds.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513662-no-need-to-kungfu-fighting-they-re-not-that-serious?p=1514879#post1514879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this is something that can be <i>solved trough</i> <i>story</i>, maybe? But one would have to establish the setting so it is <i>actually solved</i> this way...</div> </div> </div> </div>That is exactly my point. Exactly my point.<br /> <br /> (Some people <i>don't want to</i> go on an epic quest to learn a martial art. That's fine too. You don't have to start your game in the Far North and travel to the South, whilst pursued by a Wyld Hunt, unable to unlock your past memories, as potential teachers are stolen out from under you by the Imperialistic Empire. You can just say you find a dojo during downtime and learn snake style if you want.)\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-14-2023, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T13:40:42-07:00","id":1515008,"title":"","content":"It's because the Martial Artist Merit is too expensive for Mortals to afford. /j (mostly)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}